					"numinlets" : 1,
					"numoutlets" : 0,
					"patching_rect" : [ 712.0, 532.0, 583.0, 47.0 ],
					"text" : "One of my struggles/difficulties was testinng gens and gens within gens because it need layers of in and outs for debugging an dcontantly switching between screen to read values and charts its very time consuming and confusing but it is the only way to be 100% accurate"
				}

			}
, 			{
				"box" : 				{
					"id" : "obj-16",
					"linecount" : 8,
					"maxclass" : "comment",
					"numinlets" : 1,
					"numoutlets" : 0,
					"patching_rect" : [ 712.0, 93.0, 607.0, 114.0 ],
					"text" : "I would describe my sound radio as a spatial, upbeat, catchy, layered, distinct, unique variety of beats and notes working together to create music that you can tune into any time of day any day and you will never worry about repetitiveness. \nMy idea was to make two sounds a fast upbeat one and a more normal/chill but still upbeat sound, and in broad terms I did this by using 1 back beat with many params that detemermine all its charcatersistcs and 2 synths, one fast and one medium speed. So I synched up when the beat prarams that controlled tempo were higher and switched on the faster synth and when the params for the beat tempo were lesser I switched on the regular paced synth"
				}

			}
, 			{
				"box" : 				{
					"fontsize" : 16.0,
					"id" : "obj-45",
					"linecount" : 4,
					"maxclass" : "comment",
					"numinlets" : 1,
					"numoutlets" : 0,
					"patching_rect" : [ 712.0, 13.0, 604.0, 78.0 ],
					"text" : "To make this patch work:\n1. Turn on audio\n2. Adjust Volume to your liking\n3. If you want to randomize time parameters click the random date and time button"
				}

			}
, 			{
				"box" : 				{
					"id" : "obj-12",
					"linecount" : 5,
					"maxclass" : "comment",
					"numinlets" : 1,
					"numoutlets" : 0,
					"patching_rect" : [ 712.0, 439.0, 605.0, 74.0 ],
					"text" : "At first I made it so the changes got more drastic over time like small changes for seconds and minutes and medium ones for hours then big one for days and motnhs but when testing without randomzing it and lisetening to it for 5 minutes straight I realized it gets very repitieive and boring fast so I decided to spread out the changes and make a variety of changes from seconds to days no matter how drastic I tested the changed by adjusting each time param seperately making sure the difference is distict."
				}

			}
, 			{
				"box" : 				{
					"id" : "obj-28",
					"linecount" : 2,
					"maxclass" : "comment",
					"numinlets" : 1,
					"numoutlets" : 0,
					"patching_rect" : [ 713.0, 349.0, 603.0, 33.0 ],
					"text" : "I also made a counter with qmetro 1000 and hooked it up to the seconds when I picked a random date so I could see what it would be like in real time on a random date with the seconds moving"
				}

			}
, 			{
				"box" : 				{
					"id" : "obj-14",
